Upstream-PR:     https://github.com/iiab/iiab/pull/4565
Upstream-Status: open (carried until it ships in the pinned iiab commit)
Applies-to:      roles/maps/{defaults/main.yml, templates/tile-extract.py.j2}
Summary:         Maps: install the custom go-pmtiles build (parallel range downloads), add an opt-in IIAB_PMTILES_PROGRESS=json mode (json progress + tunable download threads, default 8) for region (FQR) extraction, and pin the mirror on resume so an interrupted region download continues instead of restarting

Mirrors iiab/iiab#4565 (all three effects are in that PR). Three effects:
  1. Point maps_tools.pmtiles.releases at the custom "1.31.2-m16" go-pmtiles
     build (upstream v1.31.2 plus a small patch set): parallel range downloads
     (faster than stock even at the default 4 threads), resume/pause.
  2. tile-extract.py: when IIAB_PMTILES_PROGRESS=json is set, pass --progress=json
     and --download-threads (default 8, tunable via IIAB_PMTILES_DOWNLOAD_THREADS).
     Unset, behavior is unchanged (CI bake unaffected).
  3. tile-extract.py (K2GO-317): on resume, reuse the mirror recorded in the pmtiles
     <output>.resume journal instead of re-picking at random via get_mirror(). The
     journal is keyed to the mirror host, so a retry that lands on a different mirror
     restarts from zero.

The upstream PR (#4565) also adds a README "pmtiles custom build" section (docs
only); it is omitted here (no runtime effect on the bake). Remove this carry once
#4565 ships in the pinned iiab commit.

